            "body": "> I think that's not required. ~The instruction in readme sync with the typescript version it depends(if you check the version history e.g. 5.3.0, the version in the instruction is just 5.3.0)~ People can install whatever version of typescript lower than 7.0 to get `ts_ls` work. It'd be better to have an warning or tip in the comment instead of using a fixed version number.\r\n\r\nYes but since two month ago, when you do `npm -g install typescript` it will install the latest which is https://www.npmjs.com/package/typescript/v/7.0.2\r\n\r\nShould I edit the MR to add a comment or close it?\r\n\r\nthanks",
